    "body": "@drisspg the bot only disables flaky tests, not consistently failing tests. These issues are meant to be a temporary quick disable, and not meant for longterm tracking. So @jeffdaily it would be better to put these in the code itself so the skips are consolidated while tracked by an issue with more details, unless the plan is to fix them within a few days.",
